<p>The decision between self-hosted and API comes down to volume and engineering bandwidth. Below 50,000 renders per month, the API is almost always cheaper and faster to implement. Above that threshold, self-hosted can be more cost-effective if you have the team to maintain it. But the hidden cost of self-hosted is not the server — it is the constant cat-and-mouse game with anti-bot systems that change their detection methods weekly.</p>
<p>Start with a render API for simple JavaScript rendering. Graduate to session-based APIs when you need multi-step workflows. Add Stagehand when you want AI agents to control the browser in natural language. Each tier adds capability at a predictable cost.</p>
